version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-ZLIB-19520500:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          zlib1g, introduced by the Node base image via
          dpkg/apt — a base-OS package, not an application dependency. No
          fix published for Debian 13 (trixie) yet; base-image upgrade
          recommendations (e.g. alpine) are a separate, bigger migration and
          not being done as a point fix. Accepted pending upstream Debian
          patch or a deliberate base-image migration. Recheck on base-image
          bump.
          Re-verified 2026-11-03: still no trixie fix; premise holds.
        expires: '2026-12-03T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-ATTR-17678182:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          libattr1, introduced by the Node base image via
          coreutils/adduser — a base-OS package, not an application
          dependency. No fix published for
          Debian 13 (trixie); base-image upgrade recommendations do not
          resolve it. Accepted pending upstream Debian patch or a base-image
          migration. Recheck on base-image bump.
          Re-verified 2026-11-03: still no trixie fix; premise holds.
        expires: '2026-12-03T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-ACL-17677866:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          libacl1, introduced by the Node base image via
          coreutils/sed/adduser/dpkg — a base-OS package, not an
          application dependency. No fix published
          for Debian 13 (trixie); base-image upgrade recommendations do not
          resolve it. Accepted pending upstream Debian patch or a base-image
          migration. Recheck on base-image bump.
          Re-verified 2026-11-03: still no trixie fix; premise holds.
        expires: '2026-12-03T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-HTTPCACHESEMANTICS-19964064:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Origin validation flaw in http-cache-semantics' _varyMatches(),
          which can let a Vary:* response be reused across different
          users/requests sharing the same cache. Reachable only if got's
          built-in HTTP response caching (via cacheable-request) is actually
          enabled. Checked every got() call site in this app — the two in
          questionnaire/request-service.js and the one inside
          openid-client/lib/helpers/request.js — and none pass a `cache`
          option; openid-client's own caching (JWKS/throttling) uses a
          separate in-memory lru-cache, unrelated to got's HTTP cache. No fix
          available without an ESM migration: http-cache-semantics@4.3.0 is
          the latest version ever published (no patched release exists), and
          the only upgrade paths (got@12+, or express-openid-connect@3 for
          openid-client@6) are both ESM-only, which breaks this CommonJS
          codebase's require() calls — confirmed by reverting an attempted
          express-openid-connect@3 upgrade after it broke 86 tests with
          "Must use import to load ES Module". Tracked as a separate,
          deliberate future migration, not a point fix.
          Re-verified 2026-11-03: got HTTP caching still not enabled at any
          call site; no non-ESM patched release; premise holds.
        expires: '2026-12-03T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-HTTPCACHESEMANTICS-19964068:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Same root cause and same verified-unreachable basis as
          SNYK-JS-HTTPCACHESEMANTICS-19964064 — got's HTTP response caching
          is never enabled anywhere in this app's dependency chain, so the
          improper-authorisation variant of the same underlying bug is
          equally unreachable. See that entry for the full reasoning.
          Re-verified 2026-11-03: premise holds (see 19964064 entry).
        expires: '2026-12-03T00:00:00.000Z'